    user_response: "Build me an app with screens that look like this. \nRead the design: layout, spacing, colours, typography and any images or icons.\nTurn the colours, fonts and spacing into design tokens so they can be reused across the app later.\nBuild the page as a Next.js + TypeScript + Tailwind project, laid out to match the monorepo in the plan (apps/web and packages/ui). I\342\200\231ll write it as components (hero, modules grid, roadmap, FAQ, waitlist form) rather than one big file.\nAdd Framer Motion for subtle scroll animations and smooth entry transitions and use cool effects on the page elements where needed.\nUse the attached pdf file for context on what this page is about and the specific guidelines to follow for the technical identity and back-end development plan.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nMedia attachment: User sent attachment: /assets/aistudio/Image_3_f639e618.markdown (saved in workspace at /public/assets/aistudio/Image_3_f639e618.markdown). Read it with view_file at that path; in shell commands, which run from the workspace root, use the relative path public/assets/aistudio/Image_3_f639e618.markdown. When displaying or embedding this asset in code, reference this local file path directly. Only invoke image generation tools if the user explicitly requests creating or modifying an image.\n  User sent attachment: /assets/aistudio/METR_ERP_PRD_TRD_ERD_v1.0_f9384833.pdf (saved in workspace at /public/assets/aistudio/METR_ERP_PRD_TRD_ERD_v1.0_f9384833.pdf). Read it with view_file at that path; in shell commands, which run from the workspace root, use the relative path public/assets/aistudio/METR_ERP_PRD_TRD_ERD_v1.0_f9384833.pdf. When displaying or embedding this asset in code, reference this local file path directly. Only invoke image generation tools if the user explicitly requests creating or modifying an image.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
