  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Setup**\n\nI\'m now meticulously scrutinizing the workspace configuration, focusing on how the user\'s request aligns with the React SPA on Vite framework. I\'m double-checking every detail to ensure a flawless implementation, keeping the Vite + React runtime operating smoothly on port 3000. It\'s a precise matching process.\n\n\n**Structuring the Framework**\n\nI\'m now deep in thought about the project structure, specifically ensuring a smooth fit for the monorepo setup within a Next.js environment. I\'m focusing on the component design (Hero, Modules Grid, Roadmap, FAQ, Waitlist form) to avoid monolithic files and leverage Framer Motion for scroll animations and smooth transitions. I\'m using TypeScript, Tailwind and also looking at clean path aliases within `vite.config.ts` and `tsconfig.json`.\n\n\n**Defining Component Specifications**\n\nI am now meticulously crafting the specifications for each UI component. I\'m focusing on color palettes and ensuring clear distinctions. Primary, secondary, and tertiary colors are being carefully defined. I\'m considering detailed styles like whitespace-nowrap, shrink-0, and rounded-2xl to create visual consistency, while also thinking through specific component features for the MetricCard, WorkflowPipeline, Accordion, and PhaseBadge components. Framer Motion is also a key consideration.\n\n\n**Refining Component Details**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on UI details, incorporating the Phase 1/2/3 chip spec directly from the design document. I\'m focusing on the `BrandMark.tsx` component, ensuring the SVG\'s geometric precision with rounded stroke caps and a Manrope wordmark. I\'m creating barrel exports for the UI library, and establishing robust contracts and specifications in the `/packages/contracts/src/` folder. I\'m building strongly typed API contracts, enums, and pure domain logic that are drawn from the PDF, including document state machines and double-entry journal invariant validators. I\'m also ensuring the quote and invoice line calculator matches the specs, along with the waitlist submission validator.\n\n\n**Detailing Data Structures**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the `/apps/web/src/` directory, meticulously crafting the data structures for the application. I\'m focusing on the `data/metrContent.ts` file, ensuring its accuracy and richness, as the content is derived directly from `METR_ERP_PRD_TRD_ERD_v1.0`. I\'m structuring all 15 canonical schemas, the 108 entities, and the 7 Core End-to-End User Journeys. I am making sure the code includes precise transaction chains and real sample records for all 6 release Milestones and the 8 Vertical Slices. The erp.test.ts is also testing important functions to validate data.\n\n\n**Defining Architectural Controls**\n\nI\'m now focusing on critical architectural and trust controls, including the modular monolith design: Next.js + NestJS + PostgreSQL. I\'m prioritizing multi-tenancy with composite keys and row-level security. I\'m aligning with OWASP ASVS 5.0.0 Level 2 standards and NDPA readiness. My target is to achieve specific NFRs, like high availability and quick recovery times and include 108 canonical entities across 15 schemas. I\'m also ensuring FAQs are based on Section A4 and D6. I am also working on `components/Navbar.tsx` and `components/HeroSection.tsx` components.\n\n\n**Crafting the Preview**\n\nI\'m now deeply engaged in crafting a live, interactive preview of the METR workspace, moving beyond static mockups. I\'m focusing on key features such as a Company Switcher to demonstrate multi-entity capabilities and a dynamic Transaction Chain selector. The goal is to provide a real-time, engaging experience. I\'m building live financial summaries, including AR Outstanding, and a live Double-Entry Journal Posting inspector.\n\n\n**Showcasing the Journeys**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the ConnectedWorkflowSection, building an interactive \"Connected Movement\" that visualizes the end-to-end process, with aligned debit/credit columns using `tabular-nums`. I\'m building a horizontal showcase from Lead to Ledger, and a clickable journey switcher. Each node click will reveal the full state machine.\n\n\n**Visualizing the Architecture**\n\nI\'m now building the interactive architectural inspector drawer to complement module cards, displaying Postgres schema details and REST endpoints. The `ArchitectureTrustSection` is being updated with a high-contrast design. I\'m showcasing a layered blueprint and switchable tabs for key aspects like data invariants and security, with SQL snippets and API payloads from design docs.\n\n\n**Developing Component Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the updated roadmap, FAQ, and waitlist sections. I\'m focusing on the `RoadmapSection.tsx`, ensuring an interactive milestone selection that reveals engineering deliverables and exit gates. The FAQ section\'s accordion design is clean, with Framer Motion animations. I\'m building a conversion-ready waitlist form with full validation.\n\n\n**Finalizing the Components**\n\nI\'m now implementing the waitlist form, focusing on its integration with the Express backend, ensuring the submission calls the real endpoint with the necessary idempotency key, validating and displaying a confirmation with details. I\'m also finalizing the `Footer.tsx` with all the necessary metadata, references, and specifications. Lastly, I\'m composing `AppPage.tsx` using modules from the UI, contracts, and web sections, wrapping it with `<MotionConfig reducedMotion=\"user\">`.\n\n\n**Verifying Font Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the fonts into the UI. I see that Framer Motion is already installed. I am verifying the font requirements, which are Manrope for headings and Inter for body/controls. The integration is clean, with the `apps/web/src/` working seamlessly with `packages/ui` + `packages/contracts`.\n\n\n**Integrating Design Assets**\n\nI am now focused on integrating design assets with precision, specifically the fonts and color palette. I\'ve configured loading `Manrope`, `Inter`, and `JetBrains Mono` from Google Fonts, ensuring strict adherence to the design specifications. I am meticulously applying exact hex codes and applying all anti-slop rules, ensuring a faithful reproduction of the design with all components, especially those with `//` comments.\n\n\n**Validating UX Interactions**\n\nI\'m now deep in the validation plan, and it feels pretty solid. I\'m focusing on the \"Journeys\" section, specifically the interactive Hero and Connected Movement Inspection. I will load the page at 1440x900, check the split, and verify immediate updates when switching entities. I\'ll test the currency and ledger balance updates, ensure correct debit/credit matching and the workflow stage details, state machine transitions, API endpoint, and outbox event updates display.\n\n\n**Testing Interactive Journeys**\n\nI\'m now putting the finishing touches on testing interactive journeys. Switching to the `J-02 Procure-to-Pay` journey is working, and the pipeline nodes are updating to the procurement chain. I\'m also testing the modules grid filtering, and the schema inspector drawer opens with details. Finally, the roadmap, FAQ, and waitlist submission all work as designed.\n\n\n**Implementing the Viewports**\n\nI\'m now implementing viewport configurations for both desktop (1440x900) and mobile (390x844) experiences. I\'m focusing on responsive design, mobile menu optimization, and ensuring no horizontal overflow. I\'ll test the layouts and interactions on both screen sizes. I also need to update `metadata.json`, `index.html`, `tsconfig.json`, `vite.config.ts`, `package.json`, and `src/index.css`.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "y9b-apC_OMfMvdIPlte68Ac"
    tool_calls {
