- generic [ref=e718]: Atomic double-entry General Ledger posting engine with open fiscal period guards\n              - listitem [ref=e719]:\n                - generic [ref=e723]: Company-scoped Trial Balance, General Ledger, P&L, Balance Sheet, and AR/AP ageing reports\n          - generic [ref=e724]:\n            - generic [ref=e725]:\n              - generic [ref=e726]: Business Review Evidence\n              - paragraph [ref=e732]: Representative end-to-end customer deal from lead to settled invoice reconciles to the penny across Trial Balance and financial statements.\n            - generic [ref=e733]:\n              - generic [ref=e734]: Quality Exit Gate\n              - paragraph [ref=e739]: Zero unbalanced journals, closed-period lock verified, OWASP ASVS L2 triage closed.\n    - generic [ref=e742]:\n      - generic [ref=e743]:\n        - generic [ref=e744]:\n          - paragraph [ref=e745]: Architecture & Governance FAQ\n          - heading \"Key engineering & accounting questions.\" [level=2] [ref=e746]\n          - paragraph [ref=e747]: Every answer maps directly to METR-SPEC-001 policy decisions, accounting invariants, and OWASP ASVS security controls.\n        - group \"Filter FAQ by topic\" [ref=e748]:\n          - button \"All\" [pressed] [ref=e749] [cursor=pointer]\n          - button \"Architecture\" [ref=e750] [cursor=pointer]\n          - button \"Finance & Ledger\" [ref=e751] [cursor=pointer]\n          - button \"Security & Tenancy\" [ref=e752] [cursor=pointer]\n          - button \"Rollout\" [ref=e753] [cursor=pointer]\n      - generic [ref=e755]:\n        - generic [ref=e756]:\n          - button \"Why does METR launch as a modular monolith instead of microservices?\" [expanded] [ref=e757] [cursor=pointer]\n          - region \"Why does METR launch as a modular monolith instead of microservices?\" [ref=e761]:\n            - generic [ref=e762]:\n              - paragraph [ref=e763]: Financial posting, stock reservations, and sales orders require strict ACID transactional guarantees. Splitting ledger, inventory, and orders across premature microservices introduces distributed failure modes before operations mature. METR enforces domain ownership boundaries inside a NestJS + TypeScript modular monolith backed by 15 PostgreSQL schemas and a durable transactional outbox.\n              - paragraph [ref=e764]: Reference \302\267 METR-SPEC-001 \302\267 Section B1 & B2\n        - button \"How does METR separate a tenant workspace from multiple legal entities?\" [ref=e766] [cursor=pointer]\n        - button \"How are double-entry integrity and posted document immutability enforced?\" [ref=e771] [cursor=pointer]\n        - button \"Can a system administrator view payroll or approve their own purchase orders?\" [ref=e776] [cursor=pointer]\n        - button \"How is METR rolled out without disrupting active finance and delivery teams?\" [ref=e781] [cursor=pointer]\n        - button \"What is explicitly out of scope for the initial Phase 1 release?\" [ref=e786] [cursor=pointer]\n    - generic [ref=e792]:\n      - generic [ref=e793]:\n        - generic [ref=e794]:\n          - paragraph [ref=e795]: Early Access & Stakeholder Pilot\n          - heading \"Reserve a Phase 1 workspace onboarding slot.\" [level=2] [ref=e796]\n          - paragraph [ref=e797]: Join finance leaders, operations directors, and engineering teams validating METR across multi-entity lead-to-cash and general ledger pilots.\n        - generic [ref=e798]:\n          - generic [ref=e799]:\n            - generic [ref=e800]: Registered Stakeholders\n            - generic [ref=e801]: \"38\"\n          - list [ref=e802]:\n            - listitem [ref=e803]:\n              - generic [ref=e806]: Guided Chart of Accounts & tax policy staging review (DEC-04)\n            - listitem [ref=e807]:\n              - generic [ref=e810]: Full Lead-to-Cash & Trial Balance UAT demonstration environment\n            - listitem [ref=e811]:\n              - generic [ref=e814]: Idempotent API contract & OpenAPI handoff documentation\n        - generic [ref=e815]: Submitted with an Idempotency-Key header to POST /api/v1/waitlist.\n      - generic [ref=e821]:\n        - generic [ref=e822]:\n          - generic [ref=e823]:\n            - generic [ref=e824]: Full Name *\n            - textbox \"Full Name *\" [ref=e825]:\n              - /placeholder: Adaeze Okonkwo\n          - generic [ref=e826]:\n            - generic [ref=e827]: Work Email *\n            - textbox \"Work Email *\" [ref=e828]:\n              - /placeholder: adaeze@meridian-ops.ng\n        - generic [ref=e829]:\n          - generic [ref=e830]:\n            - generic [ref=e831]: Organization Name *\n            - textbox \"Organization Name *\" [ref=e832]:\n              - /placeholder: Meridian Systems Ltd\n          - generic [ref=e833]:\n            - generic [ref=e834]: Operational Persona *\n            - combobox \"Operational Persona *\" [ref=e835]:\n              - option \"Select role...\" [selected]\n              - option \"Company Executive / CEO\"\n              - option \"Finance Accountant / Controller\"\n              - option \"Sales Executive / Manager\"\n              - option \"Procurement Officer / Manager\"\n              - option \"Project / Delivery Manager\"\n              - option \"Platform Administrator / Engineering Lead\"\n              - option \"Internal / External Auditor\"\n        - generic [ref=e836]:\n          - generic [ref=e837]: Legal Entity Footprint *\n          - combobox \"Legal Entity Footprint *\" [ref=e838]:\n            - option \"Select legal entity structure...\" [selected]\n            - option \"Single Legal Entity (1 Company)\"\n            - option \"2\342\200\2235 Legal Entities (Multi-Currency)\"\n            - option \"6+ Legal Entities / Holding Group\"\n        - group \"Priority Rollout Scope *\" [ref=e839]:\n          - generic [ref=e841]:\n            - generic [ref=e842] [cursor=pointer]:\n              - checkbox \"Phase 1 \342\200\224 Foundation IAM, CRM, Quotes/Orders, Invoicing & Double-Entry GL\" [checked] [ref=e843]\n              - generic [ref=e847]:\n                - strong [ref=e848]: Phase 1\n                - generic [ref=e849]: \342\200\224 Foundation IAM, CRM, Quotes/Orders, Invoicing & Double-Entry GL\n            - generic [ref=e850] [cursor=pointer]:\n              - checkbox \"Phase 2 \342\200\224 Procurement, Warehousing, Contracts, Projects & Support SLA Desk\" [ref=e851]\n              - generic [ref=e853]:\n                - strong [ref=e854]: Phase 2\n                - generic [ref=e855]: \342\200\224 Procurement, Warehousing, Contracts, Projects & Support SLA Desk\n            - generic [ref=e856] [cursor=pointer]:\n              - checkbox \"Phase 3 \342\200\224 HR/Payroll, Fixed Assets, Banking Feeds & Customer/Vendor Portals\" [ref=e857]\n              - generic [ref=e859]:\n                - strong [ref=e860]: Phase 3\n                - generic [ref=e861]: \342\200\224 HR/Payroll, Fixed Assets, Banking Feeds & Customer/Vendor Portals\n        - generic [ref=e862]:\n          - generic [ref=e863]: Legacy System or Migration Context (Optional)\n          - textbox \"Legacy System or Migration Context (Optional)\" [ref=e864]:\n            - /placeholder: Current accounting software, currency requirements, or chart-of-accounts migration notes...\n        - generic [ref=e865]:\n          - paragraph [ref=e866]: No automated spam. Direct technical review with the METR implementation team.\n          - button \"Request Early Access\" [ref=e867] [cursor=pointer]\n  - contentinfo [ref=e870]:\n    - generic [ref=e871]:\n      - generic [ref=e872]:\n        - generic [ref=e873]:\n          - generic [ref=e874]: METR\n          - paragraph [ref=e880]: METR is a unified Enterprise Resource Planning platform engineered for controlled lead-to-cash, procure-to-pay, service delivery, and double-entry financial reporting.\n          - paragraph [ref=e881]: Specification Baseline \302\267 METR-SPEC-001 (v1.0)\n        - generic [ref=e882]:\n          - heading \"Platform Sections\" [level=3] [ref=e883]\n          - list [ref=e884]:\n            - listitem [ref=e885]:\n              - link \"Connected Movement\" [ref=e886] [cursor=pointer]:\n                - /url: \"#workflow\"\n            - listitem [ref=e887]:\n              - link \"Domain Modules\" [ref=e888] [cursor=pointer]:\n                - /url: \"#modules\"\n            - listitem [ref=e889]:\n              - link \"Technical Architecture\" [ref=e890] [cursor=pointer]:\n                - /url: \"#architecture\"\n            - listitem [ref=e891]:\n              - link \"Release Roadmap\" [ref=e892] [cursor=pointer]:\n                - /url: \"#roadmap\"\n            - listitem [ref=e893]:\n              - link \"FAQ\" [ref=e894] [cursor=pointer]:\n                - /url: \"#faq\"\n        - generic [ref=e895]:\n          - heading \"Standards & Governance Baseline\" [level=3] [ref=e896]\n          - list [ref=e897]:\n            - listitem [ref=e898]: OWASP ASVS 5.0.0 (Level 2 Target)\n            - listitem [ref=e899]: PostgreSQL Composite Tenant Isolation & RLS\n            - listitem [ref=e900]: NDPA 2023 / NDPC Compliance Readiness\n            - listitem [ref=e901]: OpenAPI 3.1 REST Contract (/api/v1)\n            - listitem [ref=e902]: WCAG 2.2 AA Accessibility Baseline\n      - generic [ref=e903]:\n        - paragraph [ref=e904]: \302\251 2026 METR Enterprise Resource Planning Platform.\n        - paragraph [ref=e905]: Precision Ledger & Flow Design System \302\267 apps/web & packages/ui\n```\n\n### Log (.playwright-cli/console-2026-11-19T11-09-12-864Z.log#L1-L1)\n```\n[    1014ms] [INFO] %cDownload the React DevTools for a better development experience: https://react.dev/link/react-devtools font-weight:bold @ http://localhost:3000/node_modules/.vite/deps/react-dom_client.js?v=266f9b2c:15801\n```\n\n<attached-media>\nimage/png sha:e73a817eb7101b0deef2268c5eb5e113260572dea587a4dd9d6ecac70bd07cef /.aistudio/artifacts/brain/7b2383ba-027e-43ab-8c5b-735e887be1a5/.tempmediaStorage/r1-desktop-hero.png\n</attached-media>\n"
