 generic [aria-hidden] [ref=e266]: \302\267\n            - generic [ref=e267]: FIN-03\n          - heading \"Ledger \342\200\224 Double-Entry Posted\" [level=3] [ref=e268]\n          - paragraph [ref=e269]: Atomic double-entry journals post directly to the legal entity Chart of Accounts using numeric(20,4) precision, immediately updating Trial Balance, P&L, and Balance Sheet.\n        - generic [ref=e270]:\n          - generic [ref=e271]:\n            - generic [ref=e272]: Allowed Transitions\n            - paragraph [ref=e276]: draft \342\206\222 pending_approval \342\206\222 posted \342\206\222 reversed\n          - generic [ref=e277]:\n            - generic [ref=e278]: Critical Invariant\n            - paragraph [ref=e283]: SUM(debit_base) = SUM(credit_base) in open fiscal periods; posted lines are immutable.\n          - generic [ref=e284]:\n            - generic [ref=e285]: API Endpoint\n            - paragraph [ref=e289]: \"POST /api/v1/journals/{id}/post\"\n          - generic [ref=e290]:\n            - generic [ref=e291]: Outbox Event Key\n            - paragraph [ref=e295]: reports.period.closed.v1\n    - generic [ref=e297]:\n      - generic [ref=e299]:\n        - generic [ref=e300]:\n          - paragraph [ref=e301]: Modular Domain Inventory \302\267 Section B5 & C7\n          - heading \"15 isolated schemas. One coherent data model.\" [level=2] [ref=e302]\n          - paragraph [ref=e303]: Every module owns its aggregate rules and PostgreSQL tables. Cross-module writes orchestrate atomically without uncontrolled table mutations. Click any domain to inspect its canonical entities and REST contract.\n        - generic [ref=e304]:\n          - group \"Filter modules by rollout phase\" [ref=e305]:\n            - button \"All Domains\" [pressed] [ref=e306] [cursor=pointer]\n            - \'button \"Phase 1: Core\" [ref=e307] [cursor=pointer]\'\n            - \'button \"Phase 2: Operations\" [ref=e308] [cursor=pointer]\'\n            - \'button \"Phase 3: Expansion\" [ref=e309] [cursor=pointer]\'\n          - paragraph [ref=e310]: Showing 12 domain groups \302\267 108 canonical entities\n      - generic [ref=e311]:\n        - button \"core.* Phase 1 Core IAM & Party Registry Multi-tenant isolation, legal entities, branches, RBAC with server-side scope checks, deduplicated customer/vendor parties, atomic document numbering, and append-only audit logs. 18 tables P0 CORE-01 Inspect schema\" [ref=e312] [cursor=pointer]:\n          - generic [ref=e313]:\n            - generic [ref=e314]:\n              - generic [ref=e315]: core.*\n              - generic [ref=e316]: Phase 1\n            - generic [ref=e317]:\n              - heading \"Core IAM & Party Registry\" [level=3] [ref=e318]\n              - paragraph [ref=e319]: Multi-tenant isolation, legal entities, branches, RBAC with server-side scope checks, deduplicated customer/vendor parties, atomic document numbering, and append-only audit logs.\n          - generic [ref=e320]:\n            - generic [ref=e321]:\n              - generic [ref=e322]: 18 tables\n              - generic [aria-hidden] [ref=e323]: \302\267\n              - generic [ref=e324]: P0\n              - generic [aria-hidden] [ref=e325]: \302\267\n              - generic [ref=e326]: CORE-01\n            - generic [ref=e327]: Inspect schema\n        - button \"finance.* Phase 1 Finance & General Ledger Posting-grade double-entry GL, fiscal period locks, company-scoped Chart of Accounts, numbered customer invoices, vendor bills, payment allocations, FX rates, and Trial Balance / P&L reporting. 19 tables P0 FIN-01 Inspect schema\" [ref=e331] [cursor=pointer]:\n          - generic [ref=e332]:\n            - generic [ref=e333]:\n              - generic [ref=e334]: finance.*\n              - generic [ref=e335]: Phase 1\n            - generic [ref=e336]:\n              - heading \"Finance & General Ledger\" [level=3] [ref=e337]\n              - paragraph [ref=e338]: Posting-grade double-entry GL, fiscal period locks, company-scoped Chart of Accounts, numbered customer invoices, vendor bills, payment allocations, FX rates, and Trial Balance / P&L reporting.\n          - generic [ref=e339]:\n            - generic [ref=e340]:\n              - generic [ref=e341]: 19 tables\n              - generic [aria-hidden] [ref=e342]: \302\267\n              - generic [ref=e343]: P0\n              - generic [aria-hidden] [ref=e344]: \302\267\n              - generic [ref=e345]: FIN-01\n            - generic [ref=e346]: Inspect schema\n        - button \"sales.* Phase 1 Sales, Quotes & Orders Versioned commercial quotations with immutable line/tax snapshots, approval gates, pricing permission validation, and traceable order conversion. 5 tables P0 SAL-01 Inspect schema\" [ref=e350] [cursor=pointer]:\n          - generic [ref=e351]:\n            - generic [ref=e352]:\n              - generic [ref=e353]: sales.*\n              - generic [ref=e354]: Phase 1\n            - generic [ref=e355]:\n              - heading \"Sales, Quotes & Orders\" [level=3] [ref=e356]\n              - paragraph [ref=e357]: Versioned commercial quotations with immutable line/tax snapshots, approval gates, pricing permission validation, and traceable order conversion.\n          - generic [ref=e358]:\n            - generic [ref=e359]:\n              - generic [ref=e360]: 5 tables\n              - generic [aria-hidden] [ref=e361]: \302\267\n              - generic [ref=e362]: P0\n              - generic [aria-hidden] [ref=e363]: \302\267\n              - generic [ref=e364]: SAL-01\n            - generic [ref=e365]: Inspect schema\n        - button \"crm.* Phase 1 CRM & Pipeline Lead intake and deduplicated qualification, weighted opportunity pipelines, item estimates, win/loss tracking, and scoped owner/team forecasts. 5 tables P0 CRM-01 Inspect schema\" [ref=e369] [cursor=pointer]:\n          - generic [ref=e370]:\n            - generic [ref=e371]:\n              - generic [ref=e372]: crm.*\n              - generic [