l=4] [ref=e709]\n            - list [ref=e710]:\n              - listitem [ref=e711]:\n                - generic [ref=e715]: Numbered customer invoices, partial/multi-invoice payment allocations, and manual vendor bills\n              - listitem [ref=e716]:\n                - generic [ref=e720]: Atomic double-entry General Ledger posting engine with open fiscal period guards\n              - listitem [ref=e721]:\n                - generic [ref=e725]: Company-scoped Trial Balance, General Ledger, P&L, Balance Sheet, and AR/AP ageing reports\n          - generic [ref=e726]:\n            - generic [ref=e727]:\n              - generic [ref=e728]: Business Review Evidence\n              - paragraph [ref=e734]: Representative end-to-end customer deal from lead to settled invoice reconciles to the penny across Trial Balance and financial statements.\n            - generic [ref=e735]:\n              - generic [ref=e736]: Quality Exit Gate\n              - paragraph [ref=e741]: Zero unbalanced journals, closed-period lock verified, OWASP ASVS L2 triage closed.\n    - generic [ref=e744]:\n      - generic [ref=e745]:\n        - generic [ref=e746]:\n          - paragraph [ref=e747]: Architecture & Governance FAQ\n          - heading \"Key engineering & accounting questions.\" [level=2] [ref=e748]\n          - paragraph [ref=e749]: Every answer maps directly to METR-SPEC-001 policy decisions, accounting invariants, and OWASP ASVS security controls.\n        - group \"Filter FAQ by topic\" [ref=e750]:\n          - button \"All\" [pressed] [ref=e751] [cursor=pointer]\n          - button \"Architecture\" [ref=e752] [cursor=pointer]\n          - button \"Finance & Ledger\" [ref=e753] [cursor=pointer]\n          - button \"Security & Tenancy\" [ref=e754] [cursor=pointer]\n          - button \"Rollout\" [ref=e755] [cursor=pointer]\n      - generic [ref=e757]:\n        - generic [ref=e758]:\n          - button \"Why does METR launch as a modular monolith instead of microservices?\" [expanded] [ref=e759] [cursor=pointer]\n          - region \"Why does METR launch as a modular monolith instead of microservices?\" [ref=e763]:\n            - generic [ref=e764]:\n              - paragraph [ref=e765]: Financial posting, stock reservations, and sales orders require strict ACID transactional guarantees. Splitting ledger, inventory, and orders across premature microservices introduces distributed failure modes before operations mature. METR enforces domain ownership boundaries inside a NestJS + TypeScript modular monolith backed by 15 PostgreSQL schemas and a durable transactional outbox.\n              - paragraph [ref=e766]: Reference \302\267 METR-SPEC-001 \302\267 Section B1 & B2\n        - button \"How does METR separate a tenant workspace from multiple legal entities?\" [ref=e768] [cursor=pointer]\n        - button \"How are double-entry integrity and posted document immutability enforced?\" [ref=e773] [cursor=pointer]\n        - button \"Can a system administrator view payroll or approve their own purchase orders?\" [ref=e778] [cursor=pointer]\n        - button \"How is METR rolled out without disrupting active finance and delivery teams?\" [ref=e783] [cursor=pointer]\n        - button \"What is explicitly out of scope for the initial Phase 1 release?\" [ref=e788] [cursor=pointer]\n    - generic [ref=e794]:\n      - generic [ref=e795]:\n        - generic [ref=e796]:\n          - paragraph [ref=e797]: Early Access & Stakeholder Pilot\n          - heading \"Reserve a Phase 1 workspace onboarding slot.\" [level=2] [ref=e798]\n          - paragraph [ref=e799]: Join finance leaders, operations directors, and engineering teams validating METR across multi-entity lead-to-cash and general ledger pilots.\n        - generic [ref=e800]:\n          - generic [ref=e801]:\n            - generic [ref=e802]: Registered Stakeholders\n            - generic [ref=e803]: \"38\"\n          - list [ref=e804]:\n            - listitem [ref=e805]:\n              - generic [