ref=e756] [cursor=pointer]\n      - generic [ref=e758]:\n        - generic [ref=e759]:\n          - button \"Why does METR launch as a modular monolith instead of microservices?\" [expanded] [ref=e760] [cursor=pointer]\n          - region \"Why does METR launch as a modular monolith instead of microservices?\" [ref=e764]:\n            - generic [ref=e765]:\n              - paragraph [ref=e766]: Financial posting, stock reservations, and sales orders require strict ACID transactional guarantees. Splitting ledger, inventory, and orders across premature microservices introduces distributed failure modes before operations mature. METR enforces domain ownership boundaries inside a NestJS + TypeScript modular monolith backed by 15 PostgreSQL schemas and a durable transactional outbox.\n              - paragraph [ref=e767]: Reference \302\267 METR-SPEC-001 \302\267 Section B1 & B2\n        - button \"How does METR separate a tenant workspace from multiple legal entities?\" [ref=e769] [cursor=pointer]\n        - button \"How are double-entry integrity and posted document immutability enforced?\" [ref=e774] [cursor=pointer]\n        - button \"Can a system administrator view payroll or approve their own purchase orders?\" [ref=e779] [cursor=pointer]\n        - button \"How is METR rolled out without disrupting active finance and delivery teams?\" [ref=e784] [cursor=pointer]\n        - button \"What is explicitly out of scope for the initial Phase 1 release?\" [ref=e789] [cursor=pointer]\n    - generic [ref=e795]:\n      - generic [ref=e796]:\n        - generic [ref=e797]:\n          - paragraph [ref=e798]: Early Access & Stakeholder Pilot\n          - heading \"Reserve a Phase 1 workspace onboarding slot.\" [level=2] [ref=e799]\n          - paragraph [ref=e800]: Join finance leaders, operations directors, and engineering teams validating METR across multi-entity lead-to-cash and general ledger pilots.\n        - generic [ref=e801]:\n          - generic [ref=e802]:\n         