    response: "I have built the **METR Enterprise Resource Planning Platform** web application following the **Precision Ledger & Flow** design system and the **METR-SPEC-001 (v1.0)** PRD/TRD/ERD specification.\n\n### Architecture & Monorepo Layout\n- **Design Tokens & Shared UI (`packages/ui`)**: Translated the color hierarchy (`#0F766E` Primary Teal, `#102A43` Secondary Navy, `#2DD4BF` Tertiary Mint accelerator, `#172B4D` Neutral Ink, `#F5F7FA` Canvas, `#FFFFFF` Surface, `#0B1724` Dark Surface), `Manrope` + `Inter` + `JetBrains Mono` typography with tabular numerals (`tnum` + `zero`), 8px spacing rhythm, and Rounded Level 2 elevation into both Tailwind v4 `@theme` CSS tokens and typed TypeScript tokens (`metrTokens`), alongside reusable `BrandMark`, `Button`, `PhaseBadge`, `MetricCard`, `WorkflowPipeline`, `Accordion`, and `Reveal` components.\n- **Domain Contracts & Invariants (`packages/contracts`)**: Implemented fixed-point (`numeric(20,4)`) decimal math, double-entry journal balance and open fiscal period validation (Section B7), document state transition guards (Section A7), and waitlist validation contracts.\n- **Modular Web App (`apps/web`)**: Built as focused components with Motion scroll and entry transitions (`MotionConfig reducedMotion=\"user\"`):\n  - **Navigation Bar**: Three-zone top bar with subtle scroll progress track and responsive mobile drawer.\n  - **Hero & Live Ledger Workspace Preview**: 5:7 desktop grid featuring a live multi-entity preview (`Meridian NG (NGN)` / `Meridian UK (GBP)`), interactive payment allocation, quote/invoice line snapshot toggle, and a live double-entry imbalance guard (`UAT-04`).\n  - **Connected Movement Pipeline**: Interactive lifecycle flows for `J-01 Lead-to-Cash`, `J-02 Procure-to-Pay`, and `J-03 Contract-to-Renewal`, inspecting state machines, invariants, `/api/v1` endpoints, and outbox event keys.\n  - **Modules Grid & Schema Inspector**: All 15 canonical PostgreSQL schemas / 108 entities grouped by Phase 1, Phase 2, and Phase 3 with interactive phase filtering and an expandable dark schema/boundary inspector.\n  - **Technical Identity & Trust Section**: Secondary Navy & Dark Surface architectural overview with switchable tabs for PostgreSQL SQL patterns, monorepo blueprint, sample `/api/v1/quotes` payload, OWASP ASVS / NDPA controls, and NFR baseline metrics.\n  - **Roadmap & FAQ**: Toggleable view between Release Milestones (`M0\342\200\223M5`) and Vertical Slices (`0\342\200\2237`), plus a topic-filterable FAQ accordion.\n  - **Early Access Waitlist & Express API (`server.ts`)**: Validated pilot request form backed by `GET /api/v1/waitlist/count` and `POST /api/v1/waitlist` with `Idempotency-Key` deduplication and METR standard response envelopes.\n\n### Verification Summary\n- **Unit Tests**: All 5 `node:test` tests in `packages/contracts` passed (balanced journals, unbalanced & closed-period rejection, fixed-point quote totals, state transitions, and waitlist validation).\n- **Build & Type Check**: `compile_applet` (Vite production build) and `lint_applet` (`tsc --noEmit`) passed with zero errors.\n- **Browser Verification (1440\303\227900 Desktop & 390\303\227844 Mobile)**: Verified zero console errors, `200`/`201` API responses, and all interactive journeys (entity switching, imbalance guard, workflow stage selection, module phase filtering and schema inspection, roadmap slice toggle, FAQ expansion, and waitlist validation + submission).\n- **Fixes Applied from Visual Inspection**: Refined the hero proof strip into a balanced 3-column grid, tightened the workspace toolbar onto a single desktop row, added smooth scroll-into-view for the module schema inspector, added screen-reader spacing on journey switcher labels, and resolved mobile 390px right-edge wrapping on the proof strip and legal-entity switcher.\n\n*Note on runtime stack*: To run natively within this workspace\'s Vite + Express environment on port 3000 while matching the METR repository blueprint, the app uses the `apps/web`, `packages/ui`, and `packages/contracts` monorepo structure mounted through Vite and Express rather than a separate Next.js build process, and stores waitlist submissions in memory on the Express server."
    thinking: "**Observing Flawless Details**\n\nI\'m struck by the pristine rendering of the UI elements. Specifically, the clarity of \'15 / PostgreSQL Schemas\', \'108 / Canonical Entities\', and \'numeric(20,4) / Ledger Precision\' is remarkable. The dark Navy \'Legal Entity Scope\' switcher also caught my eye as well, with no visible imperfections.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "r9r-atgvlIbGzQ-Fvb-YDw"
