  user_input {
    user_response: "First off let\'s use this attached metrM.svg as the \"M\" in the higlighted \"METR\" elements.\nSecondly lets put the highlighted icons(the svg) and texts(the \"METR\") in the header and footer each together to look like 1 word(as a brand logo). The idea is for it to look like \"3METR\"(The \"3\" is the metr-mark.svg file, the \"M\" is the attached metrM.svg file(without the light gray border and the \"ETR\" will just be the rest of the existing \"ETR text there.\nApply style changes to the selected element(s).\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nMedia attachment: User sent attachment: /assets/aistudio/metrM_1da0b7b9.svg (saved in workspace at /public/assets/aistudio/metrM_1da0b7b9.svg). Read it with view_file at that path; in shell commands, which run from the workspace root, use the relative path public/assets/aistudio/metrM_1da0b7b9.svg. When displaying or embedding this asset in code, reference this local file path directly. Only invoke image generation tools if the user explicitly requests creating or modifying an image.\nCSS selector 1: div#root:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > header:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(2) > a:nth-of-type(1) > span:nth-of-type(1) > span:nth-of-type(1)\nCSS 1: {\n\n}\nCSS selector 2: div#root:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > header:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(2) > a:nth-of-type(1) > span:nth-of-type(1) > img:nth-of-type(1)\nCSS 2: {\n\n}\nCSS selector 3: div#root:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > footer:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > span:nth-of-type(1) > span:nth-of-type(1)\nCSS 3: {\n\n}\nCSS selector 4: div#root:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > footer:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > span:nth-of-type(1) > img:nth-of-type(1)\nCSS 4: {\n\n}\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    items {
      text: "First off let\'s use this attached metrM.svg as the \"M\" in the higlighted \"METR\" elements.\nSecondly lets put the highlighted icons(the svg) and texts(the \"METR\") in the header and footer each together to look like 1 word(as a brand logo). The idea is for it to look like \"3METR\"(The \"3\" is the metr-mark.svg file, the \"M\" is the attached metrM.svg file(without the light gray border and the \"ETR\" will just be the rest of the existing \"ETR text there.\nApply style changes to the selected element(s).\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nMedia attachment: User sent attachment: /assets/aistudio/metrM_1da0b7b9.svg (saved in workspace at /public/assets/aistudio/metrM_1da0b7b9.svg). Read it with view_file at that path; in shell commands, which run from the workspace root, use the relative path public/assets/aistudio/metrM_1da0b7b9.svg. When displaying or embedding this asset in code, reference this local file path directly. Only invoke image generation tools if the user explicitly requests creating or modifying an image.\nCSS selector 1: div#root:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > header:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(2) > a:nth-of-type(1) > span:nth-of-type(1) > span:nth-of-type(1)\nCSS 1: {\n\n}\nCSS selector 2: div#root:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > header:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(2) > a:nth-of-type(1) > span:nth-of-type(1) > img:nth-of-type(1)\nCSS 2: {\n\n}\nCSS selector 3: div#root:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > footer:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > span:nth-of-type(1) > span:nth-of-type(1)\nCSS 3: {\n\n}\nCSS selector 4: div#root:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > footer:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > span:nth-of-type(1) > img:nth-of-type(1)\nCSS 4: {\n\n}\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
