  planner_response {
    response: "Translated the entire landing page into clear, customer-friendly business language and removed all internal PDF specification codes while keeping the existing layout, styling, and interactive features intact:\n\n- **Removed Specification & Document Codes**: Cleared `METR-SPEC-001`, section citations (`Section A6 & A7`, `B1\342\200\223B9`, `C7`, `D1 & D2`), workflow/module IDs (`CRM-01`, `SAL-01`, `FIN-01`, `J-01`\342\200\223`J-03`, `M0`\342\200\223`M5`, `P0`\342\200\223`P2`, `UAT-04`, `UAT-08`, `DEC-04`, `B7 Guard`), and FAQ reference footnotes so every card and section reads cleanly without clutter.\n- **Hero & Interactive Preview**: Replaced technical proof metrics (`15 PostgreSQL Schemas`, `108 Canonical Entities`, `numeric(20,4)`) with business-focused highlights (`12 Business Modules`, `Multi-Entity Companies & Currencies`, `100% Auto-Balanced Books`) and simplified ledger/invoice labels (`Debits equal credits \302\267 Permanently locked once posted`, `Auto-Balanced`).\n- **Connected Workflows & Platform Modules**: Replaced technical state-machine notation, REST endpoints, outbox event keys, SQL schemas, and table counts with plain-English cards covering **Approval & Status Flow**, **Built-In Safeguard**, **Team Action**, **Automatic Follow-On**, **Included Capabilities**, and **Key Team Workflows**.\n- **Trust, Security & Controls**: Replaced the SQL DDL, monorepo file tree, and JSON API payload code tabs with four interactive business assurance views (**Financial Safeguards**, **Multi-Company Control**, **Approvals & Access**, and **Privacy & Continuity**) and plain-English reliability commitments.\n- **Roadmap, FAQ, Waitlist & Footer**: Updated milestone labels (`Rollout Stages` / `Step-by-Step Timeline`), FAQ topics and answers, waitlist copy, and footer safeguards to speak directly to finance, operations, and business leaders.\n- **Verification**: Confirmed clean build and TypeScript checks, passed all 5 contract unit tests, and visually inspected every section in the browser with zero console errors and zero remaining technical jargon or PDF codes in visible text."
